<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat, 40,000 of Australian wheat and 20,000 of Australian barley in its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for August shipments.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000    Hard Red Winter</p>
<p> Canada     20,000    1CW</p>
<p> Australia  40,000    Standard White</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>Australia  20,000    Feed</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
